  "worked_solution": "The inequality $-2\\le x<2$ means that $x$ can take any value greater than or equal to $-2,$ and less than $2.$\n\nTo represent this on a number line, we draw a closed circle at $-2$ and an open circle at $2.$ Then, we highlight the region between the points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151668/assets/235e6d5bbe12a7372cd3466d877793417e5b055e6120b622f1ec52481f16bae1.png)",
